    latencyProfile: 'AirPods Pro 3 use AAC as the primary codec, the same as every other AirPods model. Apple\'s H-series chips apply a hardware level Bluetooth streaming optimization on iOS and macOS that has kept AAC latency in a fairly tight band across generations. Independent testing measured the original AirPods Pro at 144 ms and AirPods (2nd generation) at 178 ms using a dedicated audio timing rig (Stephen Coyle, stephencoyle.net). The H3 chip has not been independently benchmarked yet, so treat the 80 to 160 ms figure as an estimate built on that pattern rather than a Pro 3 specific measurement.',
